Chapter 10-6: "Quick Temper"

The prison tower fell into an uproar, people with changed expressions bustling left and right in frantic motion.

Watching the scene from afar, Subaru had his back against a slightly distant wall, arms wrapped around his knees.

"——"

Resting his forehead on his knees, Subaru let out a deep breath.

There had been too many shocking things, one after another. Not only had he been confronted with a gruesome corpse without any mental preparation, but that remains—of all people—was...

"——Are you alright?"

A voice called out to him as he buried his face in his knees, and Subaru slowly lifted his head. There stood Rem, her expression clouded with concern.

She crouched right beside him, peering at Subaru's face, and gently wiped his downcast features with a handkerchief she held. The slightly damp cloth was cool, and Subaru, feeling saved, breathed out a "Thanks."

"There's nothing to apologize for. ...I heard you saw something terrible inside."

"Yeah... that's right. There was also the fact that I didn't want to let you meet him, but just in case, I'm glad I had you wait outside, Rem. At least I didn't have to show you something like that."

"Please don't be so overprotective. I've seen many deaths in the Vollachia Empire. A little thing like this, at this point..."

"I know. But if there's no need to be exposed to it, I'd rather you weren't. Situations where someone dies because you weren't strong enough while trying to save them—that can't be helped... but that kind of death isn't something anyone should have to touch."

Subaru himself didn't deny the existence of meaningful deaths, or deaths resulting from seeing through one's convictions.

If he could deny that, he wouldn't have silently seen Priscilla off.

However, the death he had just witnessed in the watchtower—the gruesome end of Roy Alphard, the "Gluttony"—was far removed from any kind of nobility. It was ugly, abhorrent.

There was no sane meaning in taking another's life and further desecrating the corpse to such an extent.

What lay behind it was either some malicious scheme, or such intense rage—hatred—that one couldn't be satisfied without tormenting even the soul-less remains. Though he was an Archbishop of Sin who deserved such hatred, no one, whoever they were, should have to die so miserably.

"Shit...!"

Feeling a churning nausea in his chest, Subaru clicked his tongue in frustration.

It was anger at whoever had torn Roy apart, and simultaneously, vexation at how the solution to the "Gluttony's" Authority—which should have been within sight—had once again slipped away.

Honestly, he couldn't help but think about it. —If only Subaru and the others, after reuniting with Reinhardt, had hurried straight back to the royal capital without any detours, Roy might not have died.

And ultimately, Subaru had a way to verify that. In fact, if this were the Subaru from his shrunken-body days, with his Empire state of mind, he wouldn't have hesitated to do it.

But—,

"—Al."

Gripping the Al Orb hanging from his neck, Subaru bit the inside of his cheek.

Hypothetically, if Subaru were to die now and "Return by Death," the most recent restart point would be at the Pleiades Watchtower, right before Subaru sealed Al with Ul Shamac. There was a possibility the restart point had shifted since then, but based on his current feeling, that was the last one.

—And Natsuki Subaru could not go back to that timeline again, could not repeat that moment of preemptively sealing away Al as he tried to act.

"——"

It wasn't that he couldn't choose it. It wasn't because of Ul Shamac's limitations either.

It was simply that Natsuki Subaru lacked the courage to return to that scene and face Al again. He hadn't been able to stop Al, hoping for the possibility that he could change his mind through discussion, and might end up being the one sealed away instead.

If that happened, resolving the mess Subaru had caused would again be left to his companions. To avoid that, Subaru couldn't bring himself to recklessly choose "Return by Death."

But then, what about Rem? What about the victims of "Gluttony"—just as he thought that.

"...There you go again, always trying to carry everything on your own."

Suddenly, Rem said this as she placed her hand over Subaru's, which was still gripping the Al Orb.

Subaru caught his breath involuntarily. Looking him straight in the face, Rem narrowed her light-blue eyes.

"I want to make this clear. —Don't make it your duty to restore my 'memories.' My 'memories' are my problem... It troubles me when you carry it all, from start to finish, as if it were your own issue."

"—N-no, that's not it. That's not what I meant. Your 'memories' are something I have to get back."

"See, that's exactly what's wrong. Why is it that my problem ends up troubling you the most? It's *my* worry. It's not yours alone."

"That's..."

His eyes darting, Subaru found himself speechless before Rem's gaze.

What flashed through his mind was the chill from that moment in the castle city when Rem had told him, "You are not a hero"—a coldness that made him feel like he might die. Was he about to be stripped even of the right to struggle for Rem, just like back then?

"...Please don't make a face like a drenched puppy."

"Huh?"

"No, that was too flattering. Even drenched, a puppy would be cute, so your state is more like a drenched... a drenched dragon, perhaps."

"...I'd prefer being treated as cool rather than cute."

"I wasn't praising you. Also, don't misunderstand."

Pointing out his misunderstanding, Rem paused for a beat, composing her words in the deliberate silence. Then, with a "Now listen carefully," she began.

"I understand roughly what happened. The person captured in this tower... someone connected to Spica-chan was the key to restoring my 'memories.' But that person died, and you're terribly frustrated about it. —Setting aside me, the actual party concerned."

"—. Hearing it like that, I sound like an incredibly selfish guy."

"It seems you've finally grasped your current position."

Evenly, calmly, Rem carefully paved the road for Subaru until he understood. While listening to her, Subaru, who had cornered himself, gradually regained room to breathe.

Perhaps she saw the change in his expression, as Rem relaxed the corners of her eyes in relief.

"I'm frustrated too. I was on the verge of possibly getting my 'memories' back... but then seeing you, who's more frustrated than I am about it, I don't even have time to be down."

"Well, um, I'm glad you don't have to be down, Rem."

"Huh? Instead, *you're* the one who's down, making us worry, aren't you?"

"I'm sorryyy!"

Faced with Rem's stern gaze, Subaru clutched his head and apologized.

So now he was being treated as a thief stealing the right to be depressed? But it was Subaru's honest feeling. He wished Rem and Emilia and the others would never have a single moment to spare for being down.

"It annoys me that you seem to think it's fine for you alone to be depressed."

"Rem..."

"When something goes wrong, thinking it's all entirely your fault—I think that's your bad habit. And so you try to find solutions all by yourself... Won't you stop that?"

"...So you mean, don't brood over things alone?"

"That's what I've been saying from the start."

"Have you!? Well, maybe you have. Yeah, you have. You have said it. I'm an idiot for not noticing you said it! Idiot, idiot!"

Turning his face away from Rem, Subaru tapped his own head repeatedly. As he did, he felt another distinct pang of self-reproach raising its head.

After all, Rem was simply, purely worried about Subaru and had come to speak with him like this. And yet, because Subaru wouldn't properly face her, he couldn't even accept her kindness directly, and ended up making her say things she shouldn't have had to.

"Sorry. I dragged you out here all fired up, and then gave you false hopes."

"I don't think that's something you're responsible for. However..."

"However?"

"It will place an unnecessary burden on Spica-chan."

With the deaths of Lye Batenkaitos and Roy Alphard, the two Archbishops of Sin of "Gluttony" who went by "Gourmet" and "Evil Eater," the sole remaining individual holding the rights to that Authority was now Spica.

That meant the hope of safely restoring the "names" and "memories" still devoured by "Gluttony," which had not yet returned, now rested on Spica's shoulders.

Rem seemed anxious about placing that pressure on Spica—,

"Spica probably won't think of it as an unnecessary burden. ...But let's contact Abel and make sure they carefully watch over Spica's surroundings. Tell Sesshi to be properly on guard too. Whether Sesshi can actually do it is another matter."

"—Yes."

Given the tragedy that had befallen "Gluttony," the same threat might approach Spica. Sharing Rem's concerns and anxieties, Subaru decided to make inquiries to Vollachia. Determining what needed to be done, he wanted no interference for Spica, who had remained in Vollachia.

Even if he was called overprotective, he had to take whatever measures he could.

"—Sorry to keep you waiting."

As the conversation between Subaru and Rem reached a pause, the one who approached, raising a hand lightly, was Reinhardt, emerging from within the prison tower. Reinhardt had Beatrice at his side. Subaru hurriedly stood up, dusted off his rear, and greeted them.

"Reinhardt, what about inside? That Sirius woman..."

"Fortunately, I suppose you could say. I was almost certain, but she was safe in her underground confinement. The prison tower's cells are each independent; apparently she didn't even know that 'Gluttony' was imprisoned in the same tower. And it's not just her. None of the other prisoners were harmed either."

"Sirius and the other prisoners are safe... Sure, whether we can simply count that as good news aside, one thing's clear."

Nodding with a grimace at Reinhardt's report after checking the tower, Subaru affirmed.

Namely, the sole target of the perpetrator who committed the crime in the prison tower was—,

"—The 'Gluttony' Archbishop of Sin."

Subaru and Reinhardt's answers overlapped, and their eyes met as they nodded in unison.

Given the scene, there was no other way to describe the situation. However, even this certainty was not without its doubts.

"...According to what Beatrice-sama said, it's not that simple either, is it."

"I've finished verifying. Your understanding is correct."

Chin tucked as Rem glanced at her, Beatrice stepped up beside Subaru. Quietly taking his hand, she peered at his condition.

"Feeling a bit better?"

"I wouldn't say better, but it's more manageable. Sorry for leaving the scene investigation to you."

"Betty said so herself. Besides, there's nothing Betty can do for the dead anyway. What Betty can offer is only from a Great Spirit's perspective."

"I'd very much like to hear that opinion. I'm not well-versed in such matters."

Prompted by Reinhardt, Beatrice closed one eye, and the three's gazes gathered on her. She gave a small "ahem" cough, looked around at them as if to lecture.

"Originally, that 'Gluttony's' body was reinforced with Yin magic, you see. Betty and Julius worked together on it, so it was a rock-solid security that couldn't be easily undone. ...Though it's frustrating I couldn't figure out that advanced development on my own."

"We've confirmed that with the prison tower officials. The imprisoned 'Gluttony' was completely... as if turned into a single stone slab, they said, completely immobilized."

"It's something that couldn't be tampered with from the outside, let alone by the one imprisoned. To undo it, considerable proficiency in Yin magic would be necessary, I'd think."

"That's not all. Even if you take him out of the monolith, then you have to deal with Roy who jumps out. You have to fight him—"

"—And take his life. In other words, two steps are necessary."

At Rem's concluding summary, Subaru and the others fell silent with troubled expressions.

As they'd gathered, to kill Roy in his monolith state required both the Yin magic skill to undo that monolith and the combat ability to then kill Roy. Neither was something achievable overnight, nor were such individuals plentiful in the world at large.

"Moreover, they also managed to infiltrate past the prison tower's警戒網. It's no easy feat to fulfill the three conditions: Yin magic, combat prowess, and stealth."

"I almost want to stick to the conclusion that Oldbart is the culprit, including all various grudges."

Unfortunately, even the "Sinister Old Man" probably wouldn't meet the condition of being a Yin magic user.

Or perhaps if there were techniques among shinobi arts that exhibited similar power, and it was said Oldbart had secretly done it—given his ability, it might barely not be surprising.

"While it's true Vollachia has a warlike national character, I doubt they'd choose to recklessly endanger diplomatic relations given the current state of their country. In the first place, I hear Emilia-sama and the others came to the royal capital not unrelated to the Vollachia matter."

"...Yeah. Rather than suspecting Vollachia has a death wish, I'd rather believe those wolves over there have become somewhat more sensible. But anyway, thanks for everything, Reinhardt."

"Thanks? Did you have something to apologize for?"

"You went out of your way to make a detour so I could bring Rem, and then you arranged all kinds of things for us to enter the prison tower. Yet in the end, it turned out like this—ah."

"—Grandpa."

As he tried to apologize for making Reinhardt come all this way for nothing, Subaru suddenly noticed Rem's cold gaze fixed on him.

So this too was part of his bad habit of blaming everything on himself.

But since he'd already thought it, retracting it now felt awkward.

"The outcome was unsatisfactory, that's regrettable. But I'm grateful you did everything you could."

"There! As expected of my Beako! So, what do you say, Miss Rem?"

"Haaah..."

"A sigh!"

As Rem sighed, shifting from her cold stare, Subaru covered his face with his hands. Watching this exchange, Reinhardt let a small smile play on his lips.

Then, still wearing that gentle smile, he said,








