"...So, 'Gluttony' is... Somehow, it's frustrating that things just won't go smoothly, isn't it."

In one of the rooms of the Noble Quarters, Emilia, having received the report on the events at the prison tower, let out those words with her finely shaped brows slanting, her complexion noticeably pale.

The exhaustion seeping into her demeanor was something rarely seen in the usually energetic Emilia. Even so, Subaru felt useless, aware that he bore part of the responsibility for that fatigue.

—Parting ways with Reinhardt, who was returning to Felt's side, Subaru, accompanied by Rem and Beatrice, headed to the Noble Quarters where Emilia and the others were staying. There, he reunited with the members who had arrived ahead of them.

Gathered in the Noble Quarters were nearly all of Emilia's camp, excluding Roswaal and Frederica, who had taken Shult and headed to the Barrierel territory.

In other words—,

"So we came rushing all the way to the royal capital, pushing our exhausted bodies, only for it to be a wasted trip. You really got our hopes up for nothing, Barusu."

"Let me be clear, everyone besides your sister is disappointed too, and among them, my regret is top-class. I was this close to crying tears of blood."

"Hah! Tears of blood? That's just capillaries around your eyeballs tearing, isn't it? Ram could make them tear for you right now if you'd like."

"So scary! Just because you're in shock doesn't mean you need to be this aggressive!"

Thus Ram, more aggressive than usual, was also present here.

Naturally, when it came to bringing Rem to the royal capital, upon hearing the purpose, Ram had strongly insisted on accompanying them. Subaru understood her sisterly heart that couldn't bear not being present when Rem's 'memories' might return, and since Subaru also wanted Ram there, he agreed.

However, the burden of the past few months' journey—from challenging the Pleiades Watchtower to the forced entry into the Empire—had likely been heavy. Ram, who had been sustained by sheer willpower, finally had her tension snap when this matter ended fruitlessly, and despite her sharp tongue, she was now groggy.

In the end, after finishing her sarcastic jab at Subaru, she was led away by Rem and Petra straight to the bedroom, likely to be nursed for a while.

"Still, it's not just Ram-san who's in low spirits; it's all of us. With Natsuki-san and the others' troubles, the murder at the prison tower, and the appearance of the 'Divine Dragon Church'—the chaos in the royal selection caused by the person at the center of it all."

With Ram's departure, Otto, with his drooping brows, grumbled this.

He was part of the group that had preceded Emilia to the royal capital, and was supposed to report in detail to the royal castle about the Great Disaster in the Vollachia Empire, including the news of Priscilla's death. That agenda included matters concerning the future agreement between the Empire and the Kingdom entrusted to Abel—a major responsibility for both the camp and the kingdom, he had prided himself.

But now, he had been struck from an unexpected diagonal angle, left in a state where his preparations meant nothing. Understandably, Subaru couldn't bring himself to tease Otto.

Amidst this, Subaru was wondering what exactly they should discuss first—,

"—Can you tell me about Al?"

As if seeing through Subaru's hesitation, Emilia chose that topic as the first agenda.

Fram, Felt's attendant, could use the power of her blessing to send information to her twin sister regardless of distance. Using that power, they had already been informed of the simple circumstances of what happened to Subaru and the others at the Pleiades Watchtower. However, that was merely a simplified version; the details were separate.

Understanding Emilia and the others' anxious feelings, Subaru explained as thoroughly as possible.

That they had gone to the Pleiades Watchtower and searched for the 'Book of the Dead'. That on that night, Al had betrayed them and tried to harm Subaru and the others, but Subaru had preemptively sealed him. That he hadn't been given the opportunity to discuss the fundamental reasons that drove Al to such extremes.

And also, that he had no intention of ending his relationship with Al without knowing those things.

"—Mm, I feel the same way as Subaru. I think that's for the best."

After listening to his story, Emilia pondered for a while, then affirmed Subaru's thoughts, which made him happy. Her violet-blue eyes, though complexly wavering, quietly fixed on the Al Orb at Subaru's neck as she nodded to him.

Along the way, he had already conveyed his thoughts to Beatrice and Petra. So, those who formed new perspectives from Subaru's current explanation were Emilia, who had responded that way, Otto with a face like he'd bitten an astringent persimmon, and—,

"—Al-san loved Priscilla-san. I cannot say much more."

It was Rem, who had put Ram to bed in the bedroom and returned to the sitting room with Petra.

And so, the Emilia camp's stance on Al's actions was tentatively settled. Perhaps to not ruin the atmosphere, Otto said nothing—his true feelings could be extracted later along with Garfiel—and Subaru slapped his own cheeks with both hands.

Regarding Al, regarding the prison tower—neither had any leads to act on now. That being the case, if there was something left to discuss at this point, the remaining agenda was—,

"—Let's talk about 'Divine Dragon Church's' Philore person."

About Philore, an existence that could shake the very foundations of the royal selection.

"——"

The moment that topic was broached, the air in the sitting room changed completely. But it wasn't tension or nervousness that filled the space; rather, it was a thicker atmosphere colored more broadly by confusion and bewilderment.

In fact, though Subaru was the same, everyone was greatly perplexed by the situation.

"First off, what's the story in the castle right now? The premise that the 'Divine Dragon Church' doesn't involve itself in political matters, the talk of a sixth person who can make the insignia shine, the fact that she's using the same name as the princess who disappeared fifteen years ago—all of that came out of nowhere, right?"

"Um, it seems all of that is right in the middle of discussions... But the Church broke its 'rules' this time because they wanted to help the people who suffered in Pristera, right? No one can say that's wrong, and actually..."

"—She healed Kurush-san's body. Emilia-tan and Otto saw it too, right?"

"Yes, we saw it clearly. Right, Otto-kun?"

"We couldn't very well stare intently at a lady, but at least the black, spasm-like marks visible on her seemed to have disappeared."

Beside the nodding Emilia, Otto's gaze briefly flickered to Subaru's leg as he answered.

The implication was that under the same conditions, Subaru's leg could be healed too. Honestly, it wasn't a major inconvenience, but every time they bathed together, it might have made Otto and Garfiel feel awkward, so if it could be healed, he'd like to do so.

"But creating a debt to the 'Divine Dragon Church' for that is also daunting... ah!"

"Oh dear, what's with big brother getting all nervous?"

"Well, this is another case of me being scolded for putting myself last, isn't it..."

"If you understand that, then please be more confident."

Prodded by Meili, then exasperated by Rem. However, since it caused no actual harm and he didn't want to make a deal disadvantageous to the camp, Subaru feared he'd be scolded if he said so aloud, and could only poorly cover it with "Ahem, ahem" coughs.

Then, perhaps trying to assist Subaru, though probably not, Garfiel, seated on the window frame, spoke up.

"There's gotta be all sorts o' complicated circumstances 'n such. So what I'm 'bout ta say is just how I feel, nothin' more."

"Garfiel... Mm, tell us. What is it?"

"—. If'n they can heal the folks in Pristera, I want 'em healed quick, an' I want 'em ta do the healin'. All this Black Dragon 'n fly mess, it's nothin' but hardship, ain't it?"

Garfiel's plea, with one knee hugged and half his body exposed to the sunlight, was earnest.

Garfiel had a family he'd grown close to in Pristera. The father of that family had been turned into a Black Dragon by the witch of 'Lust's' evil hand during that battle, and was once even used as a decoy. Even now, his transformed Black Dragon body remained as is, put to sleep in a corner of the city, frozen by Emilia's hand alongside the other victims.

Garfiel was saying that if those in such a position could be healed, who they turned to for help was secondary, wasn't it?

"And, I agree with that. If there are people suffering, in pain, and there's a way to help them, it doesn't matter who does the helping. That's what I think."

"Hmm, Subaru saying something like that? Even though you went jumping into dangerous situations all by yourself, saying you wanted to be the one to wake Rem-nee-sama."

"Now that you mention it, I might have said something like that, but you sure remember it well, Petra!"

"I won't forget it. Because I was pretty shocked, you know. I thought Rem-nee-sama was being unfair, and also thought, even after hearing that, I'm not the kind of girl who gives up."

Petra playfully pouted, and Subaru, with no retort, scratched his head.

Indeed, before Rem woke up, while saying it would be fine if anyone did it, as long as it meant the sleeping Rem would awaken, he had certainly insisted he wanted to do it himself. A little bit, he was afraid to look at Rem's face after she heard that.

Nevertheless—,

"Putting aside my past statements, let's look to the future. ...No matter how the discussions at the castle conclude, now that it's been proven the 'Divine Dragon Church' has a method of healing, the treatment of the Pristera people should proceed... right?"

"That's right. No matter which direction the heated debates lean, I don't think they'll hesitate on that point. The focus is whether to regard it merely as a debt to the 'Divine Dragon Church' or as something more."

"The sixth person, the qualified shrine maiden... huh."

Ultimately, how to handle the position of that person was not Subaru and the others' concern.

Depending on how the people at the royal castle—or rather, the 'Council of Wise Men'—determined these matters, this camp centered around Emilia would likely decide its stance as well.

Thinking that far, what concerned Subaru was the aforementioned Philore.

"Emilia-tan met her directly, right? What kind of person was she?"

"Well... I thought she was a very, very earnest, good girl."

"I see. What do you think about Meili?"

"Huh? Meili? I think Meili is a very, very loyal, hardworking good girl."

"I get what Subaru-nii-san is trying to say, but don't use me as an example, okay?"

It wasn't that he doubted Emilia's judgment, but with Emilia, anyone could end up inadvertently judged as a sincere, earnest, hardworking good person. However, regarding Meili, Subaru's assessment was similar, so it would be wrong to doubt Emilia's perceptiveness based solely on that.

Perhaps it might have been more accurate to ask for Abel's evaluation instead.

"Otto? If you saw her, even briefly, what did you think?"

"We didn't exchange many words, but I received the impression of a devout believer of the 'Divine Dragon Church.' Sincere, considering serving others as the highest good, and..."

"And?"

"She seems a bit thoughtless at times. From what I heard, this incident was apparently Philore-san's own decision, disregarding the Church's intentions."

"Her own decision? About helping Kurush-san and making the insignia shine?"

"I understand the former is affirmative, and the latter was apparently by chance. Given the circumstances, I can only think the 'Divine Dragon Church' wanted to keep her existence hidden."

"Well, that's..."

No one present had an answer to Subaru's question of "why."

In truth, whether Philore's true identity is or isn't the princess who disappeared fifteen years ago. Her appearance, said to bear the traits of the Lugunica royal family, and that name—what do they signify. Why did the 'Divine Dragon Church' keep her existence secret and let the royal selection begin and proceed as it did.

There were far too many mysteries. Too many, which is why—,

"Hey, Emilia-tan—"

"Um, Subaru, actually—"

Subaru and Emilia's voices overlapped as they both raised their faces, about to voice their thoughts. Their eyes met, widened in surprise, and feeling as if their thoughts were conveyed through their gazes, they laughed together.

It seemed Emilia was thinking the same thing.

Namely—,

"—Don't you want to meet and talk directly with this Philore person?"

