—Looking back, Subaru didn't really have a firm grasp of the overall layout of the royal capital, Lugunica.

He had memories tied to various places: near the fountain in the commoner's district where he'd made his grand otherworldly summoning; the commercial district with the fruit shop whose owner he'd come to know; the bases of each candidate after his disastrous fight and separation from Emilia where he'd endured one misfortune after another; and the slums where the loot cellar was—but these were merely small parts of the sprawling royal capital.

Thus, the 'Divine Dragon Church's' place of worship, quietly standing in a corner of the royal capital's commoner district, was, for Subaru, like the darkest place under the lamp—as if it had been built completely outside his awareness.

"To think such an obvious church was here..."

"You seem really surprised. But a church... see, in Pristera too, we saw one where my wedding ceremony with Regulus was almost held, right?"

"That place where I broke through the door! Speaking of which, that was a 'Divine Dragon Church' too?"

With the solid combination of church and wedding ceremony, his sense of mission to rescue Emilia at all costs had taken precedence, leaving him no room to consider the background at the time. But indeed, thinking about it now, that was a church, and in a kingdom without the custom of believing in a god, it was inevitable that such a church would be connected to the 'Divine Dragon Church.'

"That said, while Wedding Emilia-tan was a feast for the eyes, that event itself is a detestable memory for me, so my impression of the 'Divine Dragon Church' starts in the negative."

"Betty wasn't there, but truly, Archbishops of Sin never do anything worthwhile. However, lowering your impression of the 'Divine Dragon Church' because of that is just unreasonable complaining."

"Well, this man's flippant remarks are nothing new."

"Booing from both Beako and Rem... Do girls, after all, dream of wedding dresses? And speaking ill of churches gives a bad impression or something?"

At Subaru's timid question, Beatrice and Rem looked at each other, then simultaneously shrugged. At that reaction, Subaru slumped his shoulders dejectedly, and Emilia, covering her mouth with her hand, smiled softly, warming the mood.

Glancing at that smile, Subaru took this rare opportunity to rally his spirits.

"Anyway, despite all the complicated circumstances that led to this outing, me, Emilia-tan, Beako, and Rem... isn't this combination, in a way, like a dream party?"

"I don't know about dreamy, but it's certainly quite rare."

"Now that you mention it, you're right. Until Subaru took her out of the forbidden library, Beatrice rarely went out with us. I'm sure Rem, before she fell asleep, was the same."

"I don't remember that, but I'm sure it must have been that way. I'm enjoying myself, going out with Emilia-san and Beatrice-chan."

"Hey—you deliberately left me out just now. How lonely, how sad~"

Despite his words, Subaru didn't mind, as this was a pleasantly rare combination.

For now, this group was the "Let's go meet Philore from the 'Divine Dragon Church'" team, bearing the mission of reconnaissance.

Now, as they approached the place of worship where the said 'Divine Dragon Church' members were likely present, what pretext should they use to summon Philore—just at that moment,

"—Oh my, stop calling me a liar already! Fine, I'll show you. This is proof that I entered the castle!"

A vigorous voice came from beyond a stone wall—from the grounds of a large building with a roof and structure suggesting it was probably the church.

No sooner had Subaru and the others blinked, wondering what was happening, than they saw it. —Beyond the stone wall, a vivid light swelled faintly, asserting its presence.

"Could that be..."

"Whoa! Amazing, amazing!"

"It really lit up! What did you do? What did you do?"

"You finally stole it! You're a thief!"

"First being called a liar, now a thief!? Just what do you take me for!? I am a sister! A bearer of sacraments! On the verge of sainthood!"

The clamoring voices of small children and a woman's voice apparently dealing with them. At what they heard, Subaru and the others exchanged glances, then hurriedly rounded the stone wall.

And as the stone wall ended and they reached the front entrance to the church grounds—,

"There, behold! This is the radiant light of our 'Divine Dragon' which incinerates those with wicked hearts! The scripture says thus: 'Man is born of earth, the Dragon descends from heaven. Those who forget to gaze heavenward and overestimate the wings upon their own backs shall know their sin through their fall'!"

"Eek!"

"Whoa!"

"Gyaah!"

Proclaiming loudly, the nun chased after the children who were running away, squealing, as she made the red light—the insignia's dragon gem—shine brilliantly in her raised hand.

Unaware of the visitors, she chased after the fleeing children with an "Oh-hoh-hoh-hoh!" while making the insignia shine, but,

"Now then, before the sublime and noble 'Dragon's' brilliance, who shall repent... oh my?"

She stopped abruptly, and the nun turned around with a jerky motion. There, she discovered Subaru and the others watching the scene, and her mouth fell open wide.

Seeing the reaction of this blonde-haired, red-eyed nun, Subaru was at a loss for words. However, beside Subaru, Emilia rustled around inside her robe,

"Look, look, I can do the same thing, you know."

She took out her insignia and made it glow red, just like the nun—Philore—demonstrating without malice, with angelic innocence, that she was the same.

Immediately afterward, Subaru watched as Philore's neck, face, and ears—all her fair skin—flushed red with embarrassment in an instant, and he vaguely thought she was just like a quick temper.
"It's nothing major. —You're welcome."
